From: Plain Browser
Subject: [safebrowsing] Drop the signin_pref_names.h includes that come back with the Safe Browsing pref hunks

Category: 70-safebrowsing. ungoogled's remove-unused-preferences-fields.patch removes the Safe Browsing and
the signin pref includes in the same hunks. We keep the Safe Browsing prefs (patches/upstream-revert.list drops
those hunks), but signin_pref_names.h stays deleted by other ungoogled patches, so these files lose that
include again. The signin pref uses themselves are removed by separate upstream hunks that still apply, except the two
tracked-pref entries in chrome_pref_service_factory.cc, which shared a hunk with a Safe Browsing entry.
---
--- a/chrome/browser/prefs/chrome_pref_service_factory.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/prefs/chrome_pref_service_factory.cc
@@ -57,7 +57,6 @@
 #include "components/safe_browsing/core/common/safe_browsing_prefs.h"
 #include "components/search_engines/default_search_manager.h"
 #include "components/search_engines/search_engines_pref_names.h"
-#include "components/signin/public/base/signin_pref_names.h"
